From: AmberELEC RG351MP
Subject: [PATCH] rk817_charger: do not wake from DC detect changes

The RG351MP uses the RK817 DC detect GPIO to report charger insertion and
removal.  Charger state detection remains active, but a cable change should
not wake the device from suspend.  Keep the PMIC wake source for the power
key and disable wake only for this charger-detect IRQ.

---
 drivers/power/rk817_charger.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/rk817_charger.c b/drivers/power/rk817_charger.c
--- a/drivers/power/rk817_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/rk817_charger.c
@@ -1030,7 +1030,6 @@
 		dev_err(charge->dev, "rk817_dc_det_irq request failed!\n");
 		return ret;
 	}
-	enable_irq_wake(dc_det_irq);
 
 	if (charge->dc_charger != DC_TYPE_NONE_CHARGER)
 		rk817_charge_set_chrg_param(charge, charge->dc_charger);
